[0.001, "o", "8;2;92;2;0m \u001b[48;2;61;1;0m] 2.1 Implement `src/domain/money.ts`: parse strings matching `^\\d+(\\.\\d{1,2})?$` to `bigint` cents without using `Number`\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m/`parseFloat`, and format `bigint` cents to two-decimal strings incl. negatives (`-15n` → `\"-0.15\"`); verify unit tests for `\"\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m7.5\"`→`750n`, `\"0.10\"`, `\"1000000000.00\"`, rejections of `\"10.005\"`, `\"-1\"`, `\"1e3\"`, `\"\"`, `\" 1\"`, and round-trip formatting \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m 12 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- [\u001b[48;2;92;2;0m \u001b[48;2;61;1;0m] 2.2 Implement `src/domain/split.ts` equal split per design D3 (remainder cents to earliest participants in member order)\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m; verify unit tests for `10.00/3` → `3.34, 3.33, 3.33`, `0.02/3` → `0.01, 0.01, 0.00`, request-order independence, and a fast-\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m    -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mcheck property that shares sum exactly to the amount and differ by ≤ 1 cent         "]
